From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] quartz, qcap, qedit: ask a filter's enumerators for the count, as Windows does (9108)

AviSynth's DirectShowSource adds its own sink filter to a graph and calls
RenderFile, expecting Intelligent Connect to end the stream there. Its
IEnumPins::Next refuses a NULL pcFetched with E_POINTER (Windows' filter graph
manager always passes one); Wine passed NULL in every pin walk, so the filter
looked pinless, RenderFile built a renderer of its own and DirectShowSource
failed: "RenderFile, the filter graph manager won't talk to me". The filter graph,
IFilterInfo, the capture graph builder, the media detector and the sample grabber
now always ask for the count.
---
--- a/dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c
+++ b/dlls/quartz/filtergraph.c
@@ -42,6 +42,19 @@
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(quartz);
 
+/* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9108): the count of a foreign enumerator's Next is always asked for, as
+ * Windows' filter graph manager asks: AviSynth's DirectShowSource (and other filters written from
+ * the same samples) refuse a NULL pcFetched with E_POINTER, and its filter looked pinless. */
+static inline HRESULT enum_pins_next(IEnumPins *enumerator, IPin **pin)
+{
+    ULONG fetched = 0;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_STRICTPINS_NULL
+    return IEnumPins_Next(enumerator, 1, pin, NULL);
+#endif
+    return IEnumPins_Next(enumerator, 1, pin, &fetched);
+}
+
